FairSplit

This product includes ideas and adapted code from:

- Spliit (https://github.com/spliit-app/spliit)
  Copyright (c) 2023 Sebastien Castiel — MIT License
  The debt simplification algorithm in src/lib/settlement/simplifyDebts.ts is
  adapted from Spliit's getSuggestedReimbursements (src/lib/balances.ts),
  rewritten for bigint integer arithmetic.

- kor-to-number.js (https://github.com/dragonteros/kor-to-number.js)
  Copyright (c) dragonteros — MIT License
  The sino/native Korean number parsing core in
  src/lib/chat-parse/ko/numbers.ts is ported from kor-to-number.js's parsing
  logic, reworked to walk this codebase's Token[] array (bigint arithmetic,
  decoy-word rejection, and partial-token consumption are original additions
  not present upstream).

- open-korean-text (https://github.com/open-korean-text/open-korean-text)
  Copyright (c) 2016 open-korean-text team — Apache License 2.0
  scripts/lang/mine-korean-lexicons.mjs mines
  src/lib/chat-parse/ko/lexicon-josa.ts (josa.txt) and
  src/lib/chat-parse/ko/lexicon-typos.ts (typos/typos.txt) from this
  project's data files. Filtered/curated for this codebase's needs; no code
  copied.

- mecab-ko-dic (via the jaepil/mecab-ko-dic GitHub mirror,
  https://github.com/jaepil/mecab-ko-dic, of the CSV dictionary sources)
  Apache License 2.0
  scripts/lang/mine-korean-lexicons.mjs mines
  src/lib/chat-parse/ko/lexicon-decoys.ts (NNG.csv, MAG.csv noun/adverb
  entries) and contributes to lexicon-josa.ts (J.csv particle entries) from
  this project's data files. Filtered/curated for this codebase's needs; no
  code copied.

- words-to-numbers (https://github.com/0x80/words-to-numbers,
  npm package @codecompose/words-to-numbers)
  MIT License
  The English cardinal-number word grammar (ones/teens, tens+ones
  composition, hundred/thousand/million/billion/trillion tiering, "and"
  joiner, "point"/"dot" decimal marker) in src/lib/chat-parse/en/numbers.ts
  is ported from words-to-numbers' constants.js/parser.js/compiler.js
  region-matching logic, reworked to walk this codebase's Token[] array with
  exact bigint/scale arithmetic (the upstream compiler.js divides by
  Math.pow(10, n) for decimals, which this port does not — see money
  precision policy in docs/DECISIONS.md) and this codebase's own tier-state
  bigint arithmetic (ported from the same pattern already used by
  ko/numbers.ts's applyAtom/TierState). Bare "a" is deliberately NOT
  ported as a standalone value-1 word (upstream's UNIT.a = 1 would parse
  "a" in ordinary sentences like "a book" as the number 1) — "a" only
  contributes here as an explicit article immediately before a magnitude
  word ("a hundred", "a grand"), a narrower, original addition.

- Duckling (https://github.com/facebook/duckling)
  Copyright (c) 2016-present, Facebook, Inc. — BSD-3-Clause License
  scripts/lang/convert-en-fixtures.mjs converts
  Duckling/AmountOfMoney/EN/Corpus.hs's example/negative-example phrases and
  their resolved values into test-fixtures/goat/duckling-en-amounts.json,
  used by src/lib/chat-parse/en/numbers.test.ts. Ported rule LOGIC (the "a
  grand"/"a buck" article-before-magnitude-noun pattern, k/K/m magnitude
  suffixes) informed src/lib/chat-parse/en/numbers.ts's design; no Duckling
  code was copied — only the corpus data and the described rule behavior.

- Microsoft Recognizers-Text (https://github.com/microsoft/Recognizers-Text)
  Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation — MIT License
  scripts/lang/convert-en-fixtures.mjs converts
  Specs/NumberWithUnit/English/CurrencyModel.json's real-sentence currency
  spec rows into test-fixtures/goat/ms-currency-model.json, used by
  src/lib/chat-parse/en/numbers.test.ts as fixture data (real-world English
  number/magnitude phrasing regression coverage). No code copied — data
  only.

- NSMC, the Naver sentiment movie corpus (https://github.com/e9t/nsmc)
  CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
  scripts/lang/fetch-fuzz-samples.mjs samples 500 review lines from
  ratings_test.txt into test-fixtures/goat/fuzz-ko.json, used by
  src/lib/chat-parse/goat-corpus.test.ts as NEGATIVE controls (movie reviews
  are not expense entries, so any amount the parser finds in one is a false
  positive by construction). Data only; no code.

- Chatbot_data (https://github.com/songys/Chatbot_data)
  Copyright (c) songys — MIT License
  Same script samples 500 Korean chitchat turns from ChatbotData.csv into
  test-fixtures/goat/fuzz-ko.json, for the same purpose. Data only; no code.

- chatterbot-corpus (https://github.com/gunthercox/chatterbot-corpus)
  Copyright (c) 2016 Gunther Cox — BSD-3-Clause License
  Same script samples 1,000 English conversation lines from
  chatterbot_corpus/data/english/*.yml into test-fixtures/goat/fuzz-en.json,
  the English half of the same negative-control gate. Data only; no code.

